## When the user is back (in this order; nothing before "continue")

1. **Kernel log of the new boot:** `journalctl -k -b 0 | grep -iE 'oops|bug:|mce|edac|bad page|segfault|nvrm: xid'`;
   `cat /proc/sys/kernel/tainted` (0 or 4096 = the NVIDIA module); `uname -r`, `nvidia-smi` (both GPUs, driver
   615.71.09); a Windows boot can change the clock or the GPU state, so check the date too.
2. **Integrity checks** (as on 10-10 evening, results/r19/integrity/): the model files' hashes
   (work/r19/integrity/verify_models.py), git fsck + worktrees (work/r19/integrity/verify_git.sh), and the engines:
   sha256 of engine-cstar161 / engine-cstar17 / engine-twin17 against their SHA256 files.
3. **Start the kernel-log watcher:** `setsid nohup bringup/lib/kwatch.sh > /dev/null 2>&1 < /dev/null &` (pid in
   tmp/r19/kwatch.pid; check with bringup/lib/kcheck.sh).
4. **C\*16.1 back on 8080:** `bringup/lib/phase_end.sh r19-resume keep` (health + one answer; SearXNG up).
5. **The 48-hour monitor is restarted after the promotion** (on C\*17), not before.
6. On "continue": `cp work/r19/queue-held-1250.txt bringup/lib/queue.txt`; start `bringup/lib/queue.sh` with its pid in
   tmp/r19/queue.pid (`pgrep -f '^/bin/bash bringup/lib/queue.sh'` after setsid). Then:
   1. **the 2-hour soak of C\*17 on 8080** + the soaked decode screen (queued) → read logs/r19/soak17.log;
   2. **promotion:** `work/r19/promote-c17.sh > logs/r19/promote-c17.log` (launchers → Cstar17.json; the rollback test
      to C\*16.1 and back);
   3. **the 48-hour monitor on C\*17:** `setsid nohup .venv/bin/python work/r13/uptime_monitor.py --out
      logs/r19/uptime-c17 > /dev/null 2>&1 &`;
   4. **B7:** `work/r19/b7_q4.sh configs/Cstar17-single.json strata-cstar17` (the Q4 config on C\*17 with tail skip 0 +
      the user's --resident-experts vs budget-66 test: exact7 items equal, B A A B, kernel check after each run);
   5. **the report:** REPORT.md "Round 19" (draft work/r19/report-r19.md) + results/round19-summary.md; memory updates
      (strata-posted-threads, the cost-gate / sampler findings);
   6. **Part D (v0.1.43, work/r19/PARTD.md):** the port → C\*17.1, the overlap A/Bs, the #1896 test + draft, the #1889
      rebase, the CMake draft to v0.1.43, the sampler issue (stock twin on v0.1.43 first);
   7. **all OK items together** to the user.

## Rules (unchanged)

One model server at a time; the 20 GB floor (6 GiB for the stand-in files); lossless only; every step ends with the
promoted build on 8080; nothing posted without the user's OK per item; the monitor is on the motherboard output. After
the RAM fault: the kernel-log watcher runs during every queue; check the kernel log after each big run and stop at the
first error.
